    <body>
      <div type="clause" n="28.1">
        <head><ref type="lawCode" target="law:VIAtr">VI Atr</ref> 28.1</head>
        <ab type="liebermannText" xml:lang="ang" source="#liebermann" n="28.1" corresp="#wit-d-incomplete">⁊ æghwilc unriht awurpe man geor[n]e of þisan earde, þæs ðe man don mæge.</ab>
        <ab type="editionText" xml:lang="ang" source="#robertson" n="28.1" corresp="#wit-k">⁊ æghwilc unriht aweorpe man georne of þysan earde þæs þe man don mæge.</ab>
        <ab type="editionText" xml:lang="ang" source="#rabin-doml" corresp="#wit-k">And æghwilc unriht aweorpe man georne of þysan earde, þæs þe man don mæge.</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#robertson" corresp="#wit-k">And every injustice shall be zealously cast out from this land, as far as it is possible to do so.</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#rabin-doml" corresp="#wit-k">And all injustice is to be banished from this land as much as possible.</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="de" source="#liebermann">Und jedes Unrecht entferne man eifrig aus diesem Lande, so weit als man es zu thun vermag.</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude" ana="#fromGerman">And let every injustice be eagerly cast out of this country, as far as it can be done.</ab>
        <note type="comparison" source="#liebermann" n="255"><ref target="clause:VAtr_23">V Atr 23</ref></note>
        <note type="comparisonPrinted" source="#liebermann">ebd. 23</note>
        <note type="comparedBy" source="#liebermann"><ref target="clause:ICn_19-2">I Cn 19.2</ref></note>
        <note type="editorial">28.2–29 are missing from D.</note>
      </div>
